  "key_observations_html": "<aside class=\"crypto-story-callout\" aria-labelledby=\"key-obs-callout-title\"><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__title\" role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"3\" id=\"key-obs-callout-title\">Key observations</p><ul class=\"crypto-story-callout__list\"><li><strong>TMMF distributed value fell 2.3% over 30D:</strong> With distributed value at $12.79B (2.3% lower over 30D), tokenized-cash balances look lighter\u2014suggesting some institutions pulled liquidity or rotated away from TMMF wrappers even if headline product news stayed busy. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/standard-chartered-hkdap-stablecoin-distribution?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Standard Chartered becomes first bank distributor of HKD stablecoin</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>A global regulatory arbitrage map is emerging:</strong> distributed value clusters into distinct compliance regimes\u2014<strong>U.S. Reg D</strong> ~40% of population AUM (e.g. BUIDL, iBENJI); <strong>U.S. Reg S</strong> ~40% of population AUM (e.g. USYC, USDY); <strong>U.S. mutual fund (N-1A)</strong> ~6% of population AUM (e.g. WTGXX). Issuers appear to anchor products in familiar safe harbors rather than one global standard. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/thailand-bitcoin-ether-etfs-draft-rules?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thailand moves closer to Bitcoin, Ether ETFs with draft rules</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Multi-chain footprints are a distribution signal:</strong> Funds listing many networks with thin holder counts usually signal jurisdictional or distribution reach, not deep secondary liquidity on every chain. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/daybook-us/2026/08/25/bitcoin-s-surging-price-faces-1-key-level-that-could-signal-if-the-bear-market-is-really-over\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bitcoin&#x27;s surging price faces 1 key level that could signal if the bear market is really over</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Rates still matter as much as product and chain choice:</strong> Rate and money-market moves can reshape fund-level inflows as quickly as any chain or product launch story. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/25/live-updates-bitcoin-etfs-draw-a-seventh-straight-day-of-inflows-as-the-rally-holds-above-usd80-000\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Live updates: Bitcoin settles in under $80,000, with interest rates headed lower on Tuesday</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Issuer strategies are splitting into two models:</strong> <em>Institutional cash rail</em> programs (low holder counts, large AUM per holder\u2014e.g. USYC, BUIDL, iBENJI, USTB) vs <em>global yield / distribution</em> products (broader holder bases, retail- or UCITS-friendly framing\u2014e.g. USDY, WTGXX, BENJI, USTBL). These behave like different businesses under the same \"tokenized MMF\" label. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/india-tokenized-bonds-digital-rupee?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">India plans first tokenized bonds using wholesale CBDC: Report</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"crypto-story-callout__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Observations rank fund-level and network aggregates on this page against recent tokenization and money-market headlines. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></aside><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
